      "summary": "This sermon of Amīr al-Muʾminīn عليه السلام gathers concise ethical and spiritual teachings, placing Islam, taqwa, repentance, knowledge, intellect, and forbearance above worldly measures of honor and worth. It also reminds the listener of the certainty of death, the urgency of preparation for the afterlife, and the moral causes of social estrangement, ending by measuring all worldly states against Paradise and the Fire.",
      "seo_question": "What does Amīr al-Muʾminīn عليه السلام teach about taqwa, death, repentance, and the true value of worldly life?",
